1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,237
This demo uses AI-generated narration.

2
00:00:02,437 --> 00:00:09,597
This presentation summarizes the V5 journal study of timestep-conditioned adapter scaling for multi-view diffusion texture generation.

3
00:00:09,797 --> 00:00:16,062
The focus is what survives comparison with strong controls and evaluation on baked assets.

4
00:00:17,062 --> 00:00:19,657
For graphics, generated RGB views are intermediate.

5
00:00:19,857 --> 00:00:26,531
The deliverable is a textured mesh whose appearance should be checked from cameras not used to generate or

6
00:00:26,531 --> 00:00:27,643
bake its texture.

7
00:00:27,843 --> 00:00:31,180
Projection, UV coverage, and resampling can change the result.

8
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:34,717
This study connects image-space scores to that asset-level outcome.

9
00:00:35,717 --> 00:00:43,346
TCAS changes the requested multiplier on an existing GeoTex adapter residual; it does not add a learned module.

10
00:00:43,546 --> 00:00:49,904
The historical C3 profile requests 1.25, 2.50, and 1.25 across early, middle, and late windows.

11
00:00:50,104 --> 00:00:54,767
In Fresh C, the shallow group is capped at 0.80 throughout.

12
00:00:54,967 --> 00:01:02,596
The realized correction also depends on the evolving hidden state, so a scale label is not a residual-dose

13
00:01:02,596 --> 00:01:03,020
measurement.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:10,269
On 300 held-out objects, C3 improves foreground PSNR over Fixed Low by 0.522 decibels.

15
00:01:10,469 --> 00:01:16,717
That comparison also raises the deep and middle applied-scale sums from 62.5 to 82.5.

16
00:01:16,917 --> 00:01:24,059
Fixed High and Generic Linear have better means than C3 across all four evaluated image endpoints.

17
00:01:24,259 --> 00:01:28,276
This revises the interpretation of the original low-versus-high-versus-low result.

18
00:01:28,476 --> 00:01:32,939
The figure shows examples, not an estimate of typical appearance.

19
00:01:33,939 --> 00:01:42,716
The specified timing primary compares Middle-high with the object-wise average of Early-high and Late-high at matched per-group applied-scale

20
00:01:42,716 --> 00:01:43,204
sums.

21
00:01:43,404 --> 00:01:52,181
The mean difference is minus 0.0339 decibels, with a 95 percent interval from minus 0.1172 to plus 0.0514

22
00:01:52,181 --> 00:01:54,619
and a p-value of 0.432.

23
00:01:54,819 --> 00:01:59,695
It detects no middle-window advantage and does not establish equivalence.

24
00:01:59,895 --> 00:02:07,697
Retrospective pairwise contrasts differ in opposite directions, indicating within-cohort placement sensitivity without selecting a preferred schedule.

25
00:02:08,697 --> 00:02:16,751
In the compatibility-selected GeoTex bake pilot, Late-high—not C3—reduces unseen-view LPIPS relative to Fixed Mean by 0.00265 on ten

26
00:02:16,751 --> 00:02:17,199
objects.

27
00:02:17,399 --> 00:02:25,005
The change closes about 3.7 percent of the mean reference self-bake gap, while substantial appearance error remains.

28
00:02:25,205 --> 00:02:32,364
A separate twenty-object GSO bake study does not detect the same benefit under its distinct protocol.

29
00:02:33,364 --> 00:02:36,798
The visual comparison makes the remaining reference-appearance gap concrete.

30
00:02:36,998 --> 00:02:40,813
Image-space improvements do not establish faithful color or material reproduction.

31
00:02:41,013 --> 00:02:47,881
The bake evaluation uses unlit base color; it does not test a physically based material or lighting pipeline.

32
00:02:48,881 --> 00:02:57,168
The two MV-Adapter timing primaries also do not detect their specified middle-window contrasts: plus 0.029 decibels on fifty

33
00:02:57,168 --> 00:03:03,614
objects and minus 0.014 on the GSO one-hundred-object cohort, with both intervals spanning zero.

34
00:03:03,814 --> 00:03:07,037
These are separate cohorts and primary comparisons.

35
00:03:07,237 --> 00:03:14,603
GSO one hundred uses the same MV-Adapter interface, so it is not an independent backbone replication.

36
00:03:15,603 --> 00:03:20,174
The contribution is an evidence chain for an implemented graphics control.

37
00:03:20,374 --> 00:03:27,853
We report requested values, cap-adjusted applied values, and state-dependent corrections; compare C3 with competitive fixed and linear controls

38
00:03:27,853 --> 00:03:35,332
and a matched scalar budget; then evaluate native UV bakes from unseen cameras and test boundaries across interfaces.

39
00:03:35,532 --> 00:03:41,765
The findings support reporting the executed interface and asset response, not a universal schedule recommendation.

40
00:03:42,765 --> 00:03:52,364
The limited public data release is archived as Zenodo version 1.0.1 at DOI 10.5281 slash zenodo dot 23383807.

41
00:03:52,564 --> 00:03:56,830
It contains selected derived metrics and attribution records.

42
00:03:57,030 --> 00:04:04,495
It excludes source meshes and textures, generated-image archives, model weights, checkpoints, and participant-level responses.

43
00:04:04,695 --> 00:04:12,694
Overall, the evidence does not identify a universally preferred schedule or establish faithful material reproduction.

44
00:04:12,894 --> 00:04:13,960
Thank you.
